$ unikraft instance shell --help

The shell runs locally and the commands you type run on the instance.
Session state — the working directory, variables, functions, `$?` — is kept
here, while paths resolve against the instance, so `cd`, `*.log` and `> file`
all mean what you would expect.

A line starting with `:` is a builtin — `:get`, `:restart`, `:mount` and the
