$ unikraft instance read --help

Read a single file from an instance which has the sandbox plugin
loaded.

The local file is always written as a regular file. Permissions are
not carried across from the instance.

Usage:
  unikraft instances read <target> <remote> [<local>] [flags]

Arguments:
  <target>
          Target instance to read the file from.
  <remote>
          Remote file path to read.
  [<local>]
          Local destination path. Defaults to the remote file's base name.

Examples:
  # Read a file from an instance
  unikraft instance read my-instance /etc/app.json ./config.json

  # Read a file into the current directory
  unikraft instance read my-instance /var/log/app.log

  # Read a file, overwriting the local file if it exists
  unikraft instance read my-instance /var/log/app.log --force

Flags:
      --plugin-name=<name>
          Name of the sandbox plugin to use.
          [default: sandbox]
      --plugin-image=<ref>
          Image of the sandbox plugin to attach when the instance has none.
          [default: plugins/sandbox:latest]
      --force
          Overwrite the local file if it already exists.
  -p, --parents
          Create missing parent directories on the local path.

Global flags:
  -h, --help
          Show context-sensitive help.
      --config=<file> ($UNIKRAFT_CONFIG)
